WEBVTT

00:01:42.770 --> 00:01:43.980
Wait!

00:01:45.220 --> 00:01:47.040
Empty cans go in the trash.

00:01:47.760 --> 00:01:48.770
Huh?

00:01:49.150 --> 00:01:51.290
Empty cans go in the trash!

00:01:52.800 --> 00:01:55.800
<b>My Umbrella Is Missing</b>

00:02:00.440 --> 00:02:01.430
Hold on!

00:02:07.370 --> 00:02:08.960
I am not a suspicious character...

00:02:09.300 --> 00:02:11.180
Bridges are meant to be crossed.

00:02:11.180 --> 00:02:12.820
Rules are meant to be followed.

00:02:13.190 --> 00:02:14.220
They call me

00:02:14.220 --> 00:02:15.650
Samurai Flamenco!

00:02:21.930 --> 00:02:23.200
You aren't supposed to put your garbage there!

00:02:23.430 --> 00:02:25.950
Huh? That's the drop-off point.

00:02:28.890 --> 00:02:31.250
<b>How to Identify Recyclables 

00:02:32.040 --> 00:02:33.130
It's still Thursday!

00:02:33.130 --> 00:02:34.630
<b>8/29 (Thursday)</b>

00:02:35.450 --> 00:02:37.010
You're so picky...

00:02:37.280 --> 00:02:38.020
What?

00:02:38.880 --> 00:02:40.490
Isn't that the rule?

00:02:41.040 --> 00:02:43.830
Okay, then you take care of it for me.

00:02:44.760 --> 00:02:46.720
I have trouble getting up in the morning.

00:02:46.720 --> 00:02:47.620
Appreciate it...

00:02:47.620 --> 00:02:49.070
Wait... Wait!

00:02:53.120 --> 00:02:58.740
And when I woke up, the garbage 
was sitting in front of my apartment!

00:02:58.740 --> 00:03:00.650
You're saying that man placed it there?

00:03:00.810 --> 00:03:04.480
On second thought, maybe he 
was one of those freaks.

00:03:04.480 --> 00:03:07.740
He was dressed funny, 
and was talking about samurai.

00:03:07.740 --> 00:03:11.170
Lately, we've received a number of complaints.

00:03:11.520 --> 00:03:15.290
A man in tights has been 
wandering around at night.

00:03:15.290 --> 00:03:17.740
He calls himself a superhero...

00:03:17.740 --> 00:03:18.920
What was his name?

00:03:19.560 --> 00:03:20.500
Goto!

00:03:21.410 --> 00:03:23.800
It's Samurai Flamenco...

00:03:23.800 --> 00:03:26.330
That was the one! Yikes...

00:03:26.330 --> 00:03:27.810
You should lock him up.

00:03:27.960 --> 00:03:30.770
Well, he hasn't committed any crime.

00:03:30.770 --> 00:03:33.560
Anyway, wait until the proper 
time to take out your trash.

00:03:33.560 --> 00:03:34.460
Huh?

00:03:35.000 --> 00:03:37.320
It makes sense to take out your trash early.

00:03:41.700 --> 00:03:43.570
Makes sense to me...

00:03:54.160 --> 00:03:55.130
Goto-san!

00:03:56.670 --> 00:03:57.960
Have you had dinner?

00:03:58.830 --> 00:04:00.480
I'm grabbing dinner now.

00:04:00.480 --> 00:04:02.310
Then you should have dinner at my place.

00:04:02.310 --> 00:04:03.580
I have curry.

00:04:03.760 --> 00:04:06.220
It's all you ever have...

00:04:10.960 --> 00:04:12.520
That's a cute accessory.

00:04:12.950 --> 00:04:14.230
It isn't mine.

00:04:14.740 --> 00:04:17.530
You shouldn't steal umbrellas.

00:04:17.530 --> 00:04:19.250
I didn't steal this.

00:04:21.160 --> 00:04:23.380
Ah, is it your girlfriend's?

00:04:25.530 --> 00:04:26.990
It doesn't make sense!

00:04:27.530 --> 00:04:31.310
If you take your trash out at night, 
cats and crows will make a mess.

00:04:31.310 --> 00:04:33.120
That's what the net is for.

00:04:33.600 --> 00:04:36.970
You don't understand how desperate 
hungry cats and crows can get!

00:04:36.970 --> 00:04:39.130
They're animals... Beasts!

00:04:39.440 --> 00:04:40.880
Yes, they are.

00:04:42.130 --> 00:04:47.040
Anyway, we've been receiving 
complaints from local residents.

00:04:47.040 --> 00:04:49.140
Can you cut back on your superhero antics?

00:04:52.760 --> 00:04:53.920
A friend?

00:04:53.920 --> 00:04:54.890
Couldn't be.

00:04:55.340 --> 00:04:57.660
I don't have any friends.

00:04:58.120 --> 00:04:59.330
Except for you.

00:05:00.730 --> 00:05:03.270
That was way too creepy...

00:05:06.170 --> 00:05:07.660
Ishihara-san!

00:05:08.180 --> 00:05:09.730
Sorry to drop by without warning.

00:05:09.730 --> 00:05:12.630
I have some materials I forgot to give you.

00:05:12.630 --> 00:05:13.660
Oh, okay!

00:05:14.110 --> 00:05:14.870
Who is it?

00:05:15.200 --> 00:05:17.710
It's Ishihara-san... My manager!

00:05:21.190 --> 00:05:22.050
What's wrong?

00:05:22.420 --> 00:05:25.340
Ishihara-san really doesn't like hobbies!

00:05:25.340 --> 00:05:27.050
If she sees these, she'll kill me...

00:05:27.330 --> 00:05:29.050
You don't have to let her inside.

00:05:29.310 --> 00:05:30.590
I can't stop her!

00:05:30.590 --> 00:05:33.430
The agency is covering most 
of my rent for this place!

00:05:33.780 --> 00:05:35.680
Oh, I see how it is.

00:05:36.020 --> 00:05:38.110
Well, it isn't like I'm freeloading.

00:05:38.110 --> 00:05:40.680
And at some point, I plan to foot the whole bill.

00:05:40.680 --> 00:05:42.000
But right now...

00:05:43.240 --> 00:05:44.490
Give me a hand!

00:05:44.490 --> 00:05:46.120
O-Okay...

00:05:48.860 --> 00:05:50.120
C-Coming!

00:05:51.210 --> 00:05:53.450
Sorry about dropping in like this.

00:05:53.450 --> 00:05:54.480
It's fine.

00:05:58.140 --> 00:05:59.530
Do you have a guest?

00:05:59.530 --> 00:06:01.710
Yeah, a friend's visiting.

00:06:02.250 --> 00:06:03.240
I see.

00:06:04.370 --> 00:06:07.020
Since you moved in, I haven't been by. 
Keeping it clean?

00:06:07.020 --> 00:06:08.220
Of course.

00:06:08.530 --> 00:06:09.840
H-Hello.

00:06:12.070 --> 00:06:13.150
Hello...

00:06:13.480 --> 00:06:16.500
I'm Hazama-kun's manager, Ishihara.

00:06:16.860 --> 00:06:17.980
I'm Goto.

00:06:18.260 --> 00:06:20.780
Goto-san is a cop.

00:06:20.780 --> 00:06:22.360
Huh? A cop?

00:06:22.360 --> 00:06:23.280
<i>Idiot!</i>

00:06:23.790 --> 00:06:24.980
I don't mean to pry,

00:06:24.980 --> 00:06:26.960
but how did you and Hazama-kun meet?

00:06:28.950 --> 00:06:31.490
Well... I happen to live in the area.

00:06:31.940 --> 00:06:32.990
Oh...

00:06:35.000 --> 00:06:36.750
Guess I should get going...

00:06:36.750 --> 00:06:38.250
Don't want to interfere with your work.

00:06:38.960 --> 00:06:40.950
Sorry about this.

00:06:40.950 --> 00:06:42.500
It isn't a big deal...

00:06:48.570 --> 00:06:51.010
She certainly has presence...

00:06:51.260 --> 00:06:52.310
No kidding.

00:06:52.310 --> 00:06:54.140
She's terrifying when she's mad.

00:06:55.120 --> 00:06:55.970
See ya.

00:06:55.970 --> 00:06:57.470
Thanks for the curry.

00:06:57.470 --> 00:06:58.650
I'll give you a call.

00:06:59.640 --> 00:07:03.400
<b>Date Time</b>

00:06:59.640 --> 00:07:03.400
<b>Hand Mari the mic 

00:06:59.970 --> 00:07:03.400
First, you hand the mic to 
Mari-chan, the vocalist.

00:07:03.620 --> 00:07:04.540
Got that down?

00:07:04.540 --> 00:07:05.710
Sure...

00:07:05.710 --> 00:07:08.410
During the interlude, 
you have another appearance.

00:07:08.410 --> 00:07:09.450
So dance a little bit.

00:07:09.450 --> 00:07:10.720
I have to dance?!

00:07:10.720 --> 00:07:12.660
Yes, only a little.

00:07:12.970 --> 00:07:14.610
I can't dance.

00:07:14.610 --> 00:07:17.040
Couldn't someone else handle that—

00:07:17.040 --> 00:07:18.290
Don't get too cocky.

00:07:19.740 --> 00:07:23.170
Do you realize how hard it was 
for us to get you this job?

00:07:23.370 --> 00:07:26.890
Right now, you're just another pretty face!

00:07:26.890 --> 00:07:29.620
It took lots and lots and lots of work

00:07:29.620 --> 00:07:31.680
to get people talking about you...

00:07:31.680 --> 00:07:35.180
Your next move will decide if you'll 
make it big or just be washed-up!

00:07:35.180 --> 00:07:37.560
This is your moment right now!

00:07:39.620 --> 00:07:42.470
I hope you realize how fortunate you've been.

00:07:42.470 --> 00:07:44.910
The agency is gambling big on you.

00:07:44.910 --> 00:07:46.320
You're expected to do your part.

00:07:46.700 --> 00:07:48.320
Y-Yes, ma'am.

00:07:49.010 --> 00:07:49.820
Okay!

00:07:50.980 --> 00:07:53.630
Let's take it from the top, then.

00:07:55.940 --> 00:07:57.080
Wow.

00:08:00.530 --> 00:08:02.210
What are you doing? Come with me.

00:08:04.190 --> 00:08:07.110
This feels different than a magazine shoot.

00:08:07.420 --> 00:08:08.590
I'm getting nervous.

00:08:08.880 --> 00:08:10.310
No need to be nervous.

00:08:10.310 --> 00:08:12.520
Today, the MMM girls are the stars.

00:08:12.840 --> 00:08:15.090
You're just an extra.

00:08:15.340 --> 00:08:16.270
Oh...

00:08:17.600 --> 00:08:20.750
But you want to leave your mark.

00:08:21.610 --> 00:08:22.480
Right.

00:08:25.710 --> 00:08:28.480
We have Mineral Miracle Muse coming in!

00:08:28.740 --> 00:08:30.220
Hello!

00:08:30.220 --> 00:08:32.970
Good morning. Good morning.

00:08:32.970 --> 00:08:34.300
Good morning.

00:08:34.300 --> 00:08:36.870
Thank you for coming to support me!

00:08:37.230 --> 00:08:40.460
Thank you! Thank you!

00:08:40.460 --> 00:08:41.610
Running for office?

00:08:43.690 --> 00:08:46.610
Thank you for coming to support me!

00:08:46.610 --> 00:08:47.410
Yes!

00:08:47.410 --> 00:08:49.380
P-Please bear with me!

00:08:51.260 --> 00:08:52.130
What's this?

00:08:53.100 --> 00:08:54.430
S-Sorry about that.

00:08:54.430 --> 00:08:56.060
Who's that guy?

00:08:57.800 --> 00:08:59.760
Are you with Tatsuru Office?

00:08:59.760 --> 00:09:01.140
Um, no...

00:09:01.280 --> 00:09:03.380
Allow me to introduce myself.

00:09:03.380 --> 00:09:04.030
Right.

00:09:03.640 --> 00:09:05.890
<b>CEO and President</b>

00:09:04.360 --> 00:09:05.890
I'm Konno,

00:09:05.890 --> 00:09:08.520
and I operate "HIGH ROLLERS HI!", a news site.

00:09:08.520 --> 00:09:10.760
I'm Ishihara, with Caesar Pro.

00:09:10.760 --> 00:09:11.780
It's a pleasure to meet you.

00:09:12.020 --> 00:09:13.520
You're with Caesar?

00:09:13.810 --> 00:09:14.940
What brings you here today?

00:09:14.940 --> 00:09:16.800
I'm here with Hazama, one of our talents.

00:09:17.280 --> 00:09:19.280
Ah, I see.

00:09:19.570 --> 00:09:21.150
He's very handsome...

00:09:21.150 --> 00:09:22.210
Thank you.

00:09:22.210 --> 00:09:24.290
And you've very lovely, Ishihara-san.

00:09:24.690 --> 00:09:25.660
Huh?

00:09:26.100 --> 00:09:29.320
Hazama-san, walk to center stage, 
and open the suitcase.

00:09:29.320 --> 00:09:31.050
Mari-chan, take the mic out.

00:09:31.310 --> 00:09:33.300
Let's rehearse that part.

00:09:33.300 --> 00:09:34.550
Okay!

00:09:33.810 --> 00:09:34.550
Okay!

00:09:34.550 --> 00:09:36.930
Hazama-san, you're a little tense.

00:09:36.930 --> 00:09:39.170
Relax, it's just a rehearsal. All right?

00:09:39.510 --> 00:09:40.720
Yes, sir!

00:09:40.720 --> 00:09:42.430
Relax, Hazama-san.

00:09:45.450 --> 00:09:48.830
Konno-san, weren't you looking 
for someone from Tatsuru?

00:09:48.830 --> 00:09:50.580
Oh, that won't be a problem.

00:09:50.580 --> 00:09:53.190
After this shoot finishes, I have 
an interview scheduled.

00:09:53.720 --> 00:09:56.200
Do you have any plans tonight, Ishihara-san?

00:09:56.570 --> 00:09:57.580
Huh?

00:10:00.900 --> 00:10:02.980
<i>Calm down, Hazama Masayoshi.</i>

00:10:03.390 --> 00:10:07.210
<i>A hero should have no trouble 
surviving this ordeal!</i>

00:10:07.530 --> 00:10:09.080
We're starting the rehearsal!

00:10:09.470 --> 00:10:10.810
<i>A hero...</i>

00:10:10.810 --> 00:10:12.850
<i>Yes, if it were Red Axe.</i>

00:10:12.850 --> 00:10:14.090
And start!

00:10:18.070 --> 00:10:21.370
<i>Smash all evil in this world.</i>

00:10:21.370 --> 00:10:23.100
Start walking, Hazama-san.

00:10:21.990 --> 00:10:25.350
<i>Splitting villains in half, with all his might.</i>

00:10:25.700 --> 00:10:32.980
<i>Coming across a corrupt city built on lies...</i>

00:10:33.410 --> 00:10:41.120
<i>It's one swoop with the symbol of justice.</i>

00:10:38.630 --> 00:10:40.490
Open the suitcase, Hazama-san!

00:10:41.450 --> 00:10:44.720
<i>That infallible, brilliant red,</i>

00:10:43.260 --> 00:10:44.990
Now take the mic, Mari-chan!

00:10:44.720 --> 00:10:48.600
<i>enormous axe.</i>

00:10:49.000 --> 00:10:52.380
<i>The axe for chopping up evil.</i>

00:10:52.380 --> 00:10:55.750
<i>The axe for chopping up the darkness.</i>

00:10:52.540 --> 00:10:54.590
Close the suitcase and back up, Hazama-san!

00:10:54.590 --> 00:10:56.080
Put on the mic and start singing, Mari-chan!

00:10:56.080 --> 00:10:59.290
<i>Kill and break! Kill and break!</i>

00:10:59.290 --> 00:11:04.730
His name is Red Axe.

00:11:07.140 --> 00:11:08.390
Did you just...

00:11:10.200 --> 00:11:11.650
Cut! Cut!

00:11:14.870 --> 00:11:16.400
What's wrong, Mari-chan?

00:11:16.400 --> 00:11:18.830
Ah, I'm sorry!

00:11:19.260 --> 00:11:20.400
Come on now...

00:11:22.290 --> 00:11:23.910
Again from the top!

00:11:25.050 --> 00:11:26.530
Sorry about that!

00:11:38.640 --> 00:11:40.080
Wait!

00:11:59.920 --> 00:12:01.640
He leaped toward me!

00:12:01.640 --> 00:12:02.820
While crawling on the ground...

00:12:03.080 --> 00:12:05.320
He was trying to look up my skirt!

00:12:05.510 --> 00:12:10.080
We've been getting more complaints 
about that man in tights...

00:12:10.260 --> 00:12:12.100
That man is some kind of sick freak!

00:12:12.100 --> 00:12:14.130
Can't you do something about him?

00:12:14.130 --> 00:12:15.330
<i>It doesn't look good.</i>

00:12:25.870 --> 00:12:27.010
Welcome!

00:12:27.010 --> 00:12:28.850
Er, I'm meeting someone here.

00:12:29.400 --> 00:12:30.850
Hey, over here.

00:12:32.700 --> 00:12:33.840
You're drenched.

00:12:33.840 --> 00:12:35.530
I came on my bike.

00:12:35.530 --> 00:12:36.860
But it's raining.

00:12:36.860 --> 00:12:38.980
I don't use umbrellas.

00:12:39.350 --> 00:12:40.590
That's odd.

00:12:40.940 --> 00:12:43.300
But I'm having a blast on my bike.

00:12:43.300 --> 00:12:45.130
And I've gotten really familiar with the area.

00:12:45.130 --> 00:12:46.490
Welcome!

00:12:46.860 --> 00:12:47.970
Here you go.

00:12:47.970 --> 00:12:49.110
Th-Thank you.

00:12:49.520 --> 00:12:51.640
Would you like something to drink?

00:12:51.640 --> 00:12:53.500
O-Oolong tea, please.

00:12:53.730 --> 00:12:55.620
Oh, no alcohol?

00:12:54.370 --> 00:12:55.620
I'll bring it right out!

00:12:55.810 --> 00:12:57.730
I'm only nineteen.

00:12:58.770 --> 00:13:00.130
Anyway...

00:13:03.110 --> 00:13:05.380
Shelve the Samurai Flamenco gig for a while!

00:13:07.260 --> 00:13:08.890
Where did this come from?

00:13:10.790 --> 00:13:15.470
I told you we've been getting complaints 
about a freak in tights who appears at night.

00:13:16.060 --> 00:13:17.680
I'm a superhero!

00:13:17.680 --> 00:13:19.730
People don't see it that way.

00:13:20.130 --> 00:13:22.740
Two days ago, you were mistaken for a voyeur.

00:13:23.330 --> 00:13:25.990
That was an unfortunate misunderstanding.

00:13:26.170 --> 00:13:28.110
With serious consequences.

00:13:28.110 --> 00:13:29.410
Did you need something?

00:13:29.410 --> 00:13:30.490
Another draft.

00:13:30.800 --> 00:13:32.010
Right away!

00:13:31.190 --> 00:13:33.360
Anyway, give the Flamenco act a rest.

00:13:33.360 --> 00:13:36.550
Otherwise, I'll have to chase you down.

00:13:36.550 --> 00:13:39.250
That sounded like a line from a hero show.

00:13:39.390 --> 00:13:42.000
Hey, I'm dead serious here!

00:13:42.240 --> 00:13:44.380
And I'm dead serious about being a hero.

00:13:45.190 --> 00:13:46.770
Here you are.

00:13:51.310 --> 00:13:52.800
Then I'll be straight with you.

00:13:52.800 --> 00:13:54.980
You aren't fighting evil.

00:13:54.980 --> 00:13:56.140
Just public nuisances.

00:13:56.750 --> 00:14:01.260
It isn't right to litter or put out the trash early.

00:14:01.260 --> 00:14:04.260
But if you tried to police that stuff, 
you'd never get anywhere.

00:14:04.260 --> 00:14:06.150
Those crimes will never stop.

00:14:07.240 --> 00:14:09.110
That isn't what a cop should say!

00:14:09.300 --> 00:14:11.970
It is for me. I'm being realistic.

00:14:11.970 --> 00:14:15.120
If you want to warn people, don't wear a mask.

00:14:15.390 --> 00:14:17.430
Covering your face cheapens your mission.

00:14:17.430 --> 00:14:21.070
I'm planning ahead here.

00:14:21.070 --> 00:14:22.630
Planning ahead?

00:14:23.190 --> 00:14:27.220
Once I'm fighting criminals, 
gangs, or evil organizations,

00:14:27.220 --> 00:14:30.390
I can't let them know my true identity.

00:14:30.680 --> 00:14:33.900
That's when the police should step in.

00:14:33.900 --> 00:14:37.640
If you interfere without any authority, 
you're only making things worse!

00:14:38.380 --> 00:14:40.790
Besides, you spend all your 
time lecturing others...

00:14:40.790 --> 00:14:43.650
Haven't you ever done 
anything wrong in your life?

00:14:49.590 --> 00:14:50.660
Umbrellas.

00:14:50.880 --> 00:14:51.910
What?

00:14:52.260 --> 00:14:54.440
I don't use umbrellas.

00:14:54.440 --> 00:14:56.410
You mentioned that. Why not?

00:14:57.150 --> 00:14:59.540
When I was in first grade...

00:15:02.520 --> 00:15:04.920
I was about to go home on a rainy day,

00:15:05.310 --> 00:15:07.410
but my umbrella was missing.

00:15:08.860 --> 00:15:12.520
I had to use someone else's umbrella instead.

00:15:13.630 --> 00:15:15.310
Happens all the time.

00:15:15.740 --> 00:15:19.870
The next day, my classmate, 
Uchida-kun, didn't come to school.

00:15:19.870 --> 00:15:22.310
He'd caught a cold after walking 
in the rain the day before.

00:15:24.560 --> 00:15:28.470
My grandpa took me to apologize to Uchida-kun.

00:15:29.190 --> 00:15:32.700
When I saw him bedridden, I realized 
how serious my crime was.

00:15:34.000 --> 00:15:36.950
In Japan, umbrellas are the 
most commonly stolen item.

00:15:37.480 --> 00:15:40.950
Many people "borrow" strangers' umbrellas

00:15:40.950 --> 00:15:42.710
when it rains suddenly.

00:15:43.550 --> 00:15:45.460
And those strangers then take others.

00:15:47.730 --> 00:15:48.820
"They're just umbrellas."

00:15:49.400 --> 00:15:51.810
That mentality has created this vicious cycle.

00:15:52.350 --> 00:15:55.220
We're breeding evil without realizing it!

00:15:56.820 --> 00:15:58.420
And that's why you don't use umbrellas?

00:15:58.690 --> 00:15:59.620
Yes!

00:15:59.620 --> 00:16:00.730
Sounds excessive.

00:16:01.400 --> 00:16:02.490
I'm scared...

00:16:02.950 --> 00:16:04.560
I'm a past offender.

00:16:04.560 --> 00:16:10.240
And one rainy day, I could repeat 
my crime by stealing another.

00:16:10.390 --> 00:16:12.570
I understand where you're coming from,

00:16:12.570 --> 00:16:14.140
but that's an extreme view...

00:16:14.140 --> 00:16:17.240
At this point, umbrella-stealing 
has become a way of life.

00:16:17.240 --> 00:16:18.770
In that case,

00:16:18.770 --> 00:16:22.010
we need to start changing that 
way of life one step at a time!

00:16:22.010 --> 00:16:26.250
The owner of the umbrella should be 
the one who determines its value!

00:16:26.570 --> 00:16:30.410
It isn't okay to steal an umbrella 
because it only cost 500 yen!

00:16:30.410 --> 00:16:32.840
You could still champion your 
cause without the flashy stuff!

00:16:32.840 --> 00:16:34.510
Why do you need the Flamenco persona?!

00:16:36.440 --> 00:16:37.760
Do you need something?

00:16:37.930 --> 00:16:38.560
A cocktail!

00:16:38.560 --> 00:16:39.490
Oolong tea!

00:16:42.780 --> 00:16:44.860
Goto-san, they're closing up...

00:16:44.860 --> 00:16:46.130
Wake up.

00:16:46.930 --> 00:16:47.810
Goto-san?

00:16:53.120 --> 00:16:57.410
I paid the bill, so let's go outside.

00:16:57.710 --> 00:16:59.880
Stop the Flamenco stuff!

00:16:59.880 --> 00:17:02.130
We can continue that discussion another time.

00:17:02.130 --> 00:17:03.860
Thank you for coming!

00:17:05.460 --> 00:17:06.920
My umbrella's gone!

00:17:09.500 --> 00:17:11.190
That was your girlfriend's umbrella, right?

00:17:11.190 --> 00:17:13.670
Yeah, she left it at my place!

00:17:17.010 --> 00:17:17.930
Goto-san!

00:17:22.610 --> 00:17:24.090
The bastard!

00:17:24.680 --> 00:17:25.400
What are you doing?!

00:17:25.400 --> 00:17:26.190
The light's red!

00:17:28.850 --> 00:17:29.830
You fool!

00:17:33.650 --> 00:17:35.200
Return my umbrella!

00:17:44.880 --> 00:17:46.250
Now I get it.

00:17:46.250 --> 00:17:46.870
Huh?

00:17:46.870 --> 00:17:48.500
I understand what you were saying!

00:17:50.320 --> 00:17:51.870
Damn!

00:17:52.420 --> 00:17:54.760
Goto-san, let me handle this!

00:17:58.050 --> 00:17:59.760
Umbrella!

00:18:09.920 --> 00:18:11.550
Umbrella... Umbrella!

00:18:28.330 --> 00:18:29.890
Wait!

00:18:30.210 --> 00:18:31.790
Umbrella! Umbrella!

00:18:39.860 --> 00:18:40.790
Who's that?

00:18:45.500 --> 00:18:46.470
He isn't here.

00:19:01.180 --> 00:19:02.490
Project B!

00:19:13.500 --> 00:19:14.960
Switch back to route A!

00:19:18.580 --> 00:19:20.470
Don't take out your trash until morning...

00:19:20.880 --> 00:19:22.270
Move! Move!

00:19:27.730 --> 00:19:30.130
Umbrella! Umbrella! Umbrella!

00:19:39.440 --> 00:19:40.570
Wait!

00:19:51.430 --> 00:19:52.330
Return...

00:19:53.000 --> 00:19:55.250
Return that umbrella...

00:19:56.770 --> 00:19:57.730
Umbrella?

00:19:58.260 --> 00:20:00.920
That isn't your umbrella.

00:20:00.920 --> 00:20:02.380
Return it!

00:20:02.600 --> 00:20:05.110
S-Someone took my umbrella...

00:20:05.440 --> 00:20:06.890
That doesn't make it right!

00:20:07.270 --> 00:20:09.520
No one deserves to have their umbrella stolen.

00:20:09.730 --> 00:20:11.080
Return the umbrella!

00:20:13.310 --> 00:20:14.020
Good!

00:20:14.740 --> 00:20:18.000
Now, let's go find the one who stole yours!

00:20:19.470 --> 00:20:20.280
And?

00:20:20.560 --> 00:20:23.530
Why did you tell me to watch this video?

00:20:23.660 --> 00:20:26.020
I just thought you might find it amusing.

00:20:26.020 --> 00:20:28.830
Doesn't he sound like Hazama-kun to you?

00:20:29.380 --> 00:20:30.970
Not at all.

00:20:30.970 --> 00:20:32.760
Eh? Really?

00:20:32.760 --> 00:20:35.170
I have work to do, so if you'll excuse me.

00:20:42.730 --> 00:20:46.350
<i>Now, let's go find the one who stole yours!</i>

00:20:42.870 --> 00:20:47.550
This is the big, new video that's gotten 
900,000 views in one week.

00:20:47.860 --> 00:20:50.560
What is the name of the hero in this video?

00:20:50.940 --> 00:20:52.560
It's the newcomer, Hazama-san!

00:20:52.560 --> 00:20:54.560
<b>Hazama Masayoshi</b>

00:20:52.920 --> 00:20:54.170
Samurai Flamenco!

00:20:56.700 --> 00:20:57.760
Don't buzz in!

00:22:30.510 --> 00:22:33.390
Wow, how did you know the answer, Hazama-san?

00:22:33.390 --> 00:22:36.050
I'm responsible for 206 of the 900,000 views.

00:22:36.050 --> 00:22:37.440
What?

00:22:37.440 --> 00:22:38.540
Why do you keep watching it?

00:22:38.840 --> 00:22:40.140
Uh, well...

00:22:40.750 --> 00:22:43.550
Red Axe!

00:22:43.540 --> 00:22:45.800
<b>Marvel!! A New Hero Appears in the Night!?</b>

00:22:43.830 --> 00:22:45.800
I guess I like it?

00:22:48.050 --> 00:22:50.050
<b>Flamenco vs. Fake Flamenco</b>

00:22:50.050 --> 00:22:52.050
<b>We look forward to seeing you
next time!</b>
